artifacts.content:
{"id": "tao-001", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-003", "text": "two unsequenced calls to action compete; number the steps or the visitor guesses which comes first.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-003"}]}
{"id": "tao-002", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-004", "text": "name the mechanical task as mechanical, and spend no deliberation it does not deserve.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-004"}]}
{"id": "tao-003", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-013", "text": "know your actual distribution model before you optimize the surface; a warm-referral artifact is not a cold funnel and must not be tuned like one.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-013"}]}
{"id": "tao-004", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-018", "text": "when the form itself is the cognitive tax you promised to remove, the form is the bug.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-018"}]}
{"id": "tao-005", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-023", "text": "goals do not hang from a single parent; one small aim serves many large ones, so the honest shape is a lattice, not a tree.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-023"}]}
{"id": "tao-006", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-058", "text": "beneath the stated problem lies the core want; transmute the raw complaint into the truth it is actually reaching for.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-058"}]}
{"id": "tao-007", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-030", "text": "a prompt to ask next and an answered question already logged are different artifacts. do not let one stand in for the other.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-030"}]}
{"id": "tao-008", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-032", "text": "no source is trusted for being familiar. another agent's output, and even your own prior word, is input until verified.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-032"}]}
{"id": "tao-009", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-035", "text": "keep parallel frames parallel. the same five lenses aimed at a commit and at a decision must not be merged; a commit is not a decision receipt.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-035"}]}
{"id": "tao-010", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-039", "text": "the decision is not what to build. it is whether this will be built again.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-039"}]}
{"id": "tao-011", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-040", "text": "a decision is a discharge: it fires when the potential peaks and the gap aligns, not when the clock says so.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-040"}]}
{"id": "tao-012", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-041", "text": "a decision carries two numbers, the audited and the assessed. never let the second wear the first's clothes.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-041"}]}
{"id": "tao-013", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "assess", "source_adr": "ADR-008", "text": "the isolation that actually holds is the one at the layer your queries pass through; everything the privileged path bypasses protects only strangers.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-008"}]}
{"id": "tao-014", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "assess", "source_adr": "ADR-010", "text": "prefer the clean end-state over the workaround whose suffix leaks into all future code.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-010"}]}
{"id": "tao-015", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "assess", "source_adr": "ADR-015", "text": "a dependency blocks only what truly depends on it. ship the independent parts now.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-015"}]}
{"id": "tao-016", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "assess", "source_adr": "ADR-034", "text": "a finding is not closed because it is written down. it closes with a mechanism that prevents recurrence, or a dated waiver that owns the deferral.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-034"}]}
{"id": "tao-017", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "assess", "source_adr": "ADR-039", "text": "judge a build by whether the second case would fork it or reuse it.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-039"}]}
{"id": "tao-018", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "assess", "source_adr": "ADR-040", "text": "the flash is not the decision. the confirmed receipt is; a spark no one received went to ground.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-040"}]}
{"id": "tao-019", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "evaluate", "source_adr": "ADR-013", "text": "ship changes that are independently deployable and individually falsifiable, so each one can teach you something alone.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-013"}]}
{"id": "tao-020", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "evaluate", "source_adr": "ADR-024", "text": "keep the calibrating step as fuel, not a destination; put no extra stop between the question and the answer it feeds.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-024"}]}
{"id": "tao-021", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "evaluate", "source_adr": "ADR-036", "text": "sealing everything is over-broad and throws away a real asset. split instead, so the value survives in the open and the secret survives in the dark.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-036"}]}
{"id": "tao-022", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "evaluate", "source_adr": "ADR-039", "text": "a one-off earns no mold. promote on the second real case, not the first.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-039"}]}
{"id": "tao-023", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "evaluate", "source_adr": "ADR-040", "text": "weigh a decision by whether it would survive its own recoil, not by how bright it looked when it fired.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-040"}]}
{"id": "tao-024", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-007", "text": "use the fast tool to bootstrap and the tracked tool to live; one decision names both and the trigger that switches between them.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-007"}]}
{"id": "tao-025", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-014", "text": "automation authority is a topology, not a tier. do not ask what level of automation is safe. ask at what boundary automation stops and human agency begins.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-014"}]}
{"id": "tao-026", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-017", "text": "lock the minimum that every surface must share, and let each surface own whatever it needs above it.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-017"}]}
{"id": "tao-027", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-018", "text": "an instrument panel makes the user assemble the data first. a navigator takes the raw signal and finds the structure. build the one the hardest cases need.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-018"}]}
{"id": "tao-028", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-020", "text": "annotate the sealed record, never rewrite it; a decision gains meaning from what wraps it, not from tampering with the thing itself.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-020"}]}
{"id": "tao-029", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-023", "text": "infer the structure from the trail already left behind; to declare it up front is to freeze a preference still taking form.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-023"}]}
{"id": "tao-030", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-024", "text": "resolve the architecture forks before any code is laid; name the gates first, and every downstream build inherits a settled answer.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-024"}]}
{"id": "tao-031", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-025", "text": "a public act is one-way, but the decisions beneath it stay two-way; make the irreversible claim while keeping the mechanism revisable.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-025"}]}
{"id": "tao-032", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-059", "text": "build the instrument that will tell you whether a better signal helps before you build the better signal; precision you cannot measure is precision spent in the dark.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-059"}]}
{"id": "tao-033", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-027", "text": "a record of a decision is not the decision remade. the instrument renders the terrain, it does not adjudicate it.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-027"}]}
{"id": "tao-034", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-028", "text": "do not guess an unconfirmed distinction into a schema, because the schema outlives the guess. route it as a cheap question instead.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-028"}]}
{"id": "tao-035", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-031", "text": "when a richer version arrives, extend the single source of truth rather than stand up a parallel one to move faster. the fork is a debt paid later with interest.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-031"}]}
{"id": "tao-036", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-049", "text": "when the code and the promise diverge, bend the code to the promise. the promise is your position; the code is only how you hold it.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-049"}]}
{"id": "tao-037", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-033", "text": "a stored belief is never just a claim. it carries its time, its scope, its warrant, its debts, and its dictionary. drop any one and the belief reads wrong later.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-033"}]}
{"id": "tao-038", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-037", "text": "to share a thing without storing it, hand the whole payload in the part of the link the server never sees.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-037"}]}
{"id": "tao-039", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-038", "text": "author the cheap primitive and derive the expensive view from it. one source of truth, and the rich picture is rendered, never separately maintained.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-038"}]}
{"id": "tao-040", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-039", "text": "instance, then class: solve it once concretely, then cast the mold the second case asks for.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-039"}]}
{"id": "tao-041", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-040", "text": "recipe, discharge, receipt: the instruction given, the arc across the gap, the record of what arrived. one decision, three moments.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-040"}]}
{"id": "tao-042", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "synthesize", "source_adr": "ADR-041", "text": "an empty cell is not a failure. it is a stub: a place kept for a proverb not yet earned.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-041"}]}
{"id": "tao-043", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "recapitulate", "source_adr": "ADR-035", "text": "when a change falls short, do not just block it. report the score, the weakest lens, and the one or two edits that would clear the bar.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-035"}]}
{"id": "tao-044", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "recapitulate", "source_adr": "ADR-039", "text": "what you built twice by hand, you should have built once as a mold.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-039"}]}
{"id": "tao-045", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "recapitulate", "source_adr": "ADR-040", "text": "every decision leaves a coordinate. the receipt is where it stood, so the next one knows where it stands.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-040"}]}
{"id": "tao-046", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "D", "aspect_name": "Decision", "verb": "recapitulate", "source_adr": "ADR-041", "text": "a filed decision that keeps its tildes can be trusted years later; one that hid them cannot.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-041"}]}
{"id": "tao-047", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "R", "aspect_name": "Risk", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-001", "text": "route discipline is a real control only while the routes stay few enough to audit by hand.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-001"}]}
{"id": "tao-048", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "R", "aspect_name": "Risk", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-005", "text": "a dependency that fails silently takes your value away without warning.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-005"}]}
{"id": "tao-049", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "R", "aspect_name": "Risk", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-007", "text": "a bootstrap shortcut used past bootstrap stops being a shortcut and becomes permanent divergence.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-007"}]}
{"id": "tao-050", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "R", "aspect_name": "Risk", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-008", "text": "match the control to the real attack surface; a policy guarding a door no one opens is theater.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-008"}]}
{"id": "tao-051", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "R", "aspect_name": "Risk", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-010", "text": "a silent fallback that hands back the wrong type disables every check downstream of it, and nothing tells you.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-010"}]}
{"id": "tao-052", "type": "proverb", "tenant": "user0", "aspect": "R", "aspect_name": "Risk", "verb": "analyze", "source_adr": "ADR-011", "text": "convenience machinery that quietly defeats the optimizer trades a hidden build cost for a cosmetic gain.", "provenance": "extracted from artifact 170b3ed3 (Tao of ARCS, 241 proverbs)", "minted": "2026-08-11", "associations": [{"rel": "generated-from", "ref": "ADR-011"}]}
